From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luke Howard <lukeh@padl.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Apr 2026 12:00:00 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] libstdcxx.modulemap: break std -> _Builtin_intrinsics cycle

When Clang builds the 'std' module (injected by Swift's Clang importer
at the libstdc++ include dir), on x86_64 with -march>=x86-64-v3 the
following include chain forms a cycle:

  std
   -> random
   -> bits/random.h
   -> bits/opt_random.h      (libstdc++)
   -> <pmmintrin.h>          (requires __SSE3__)
      -> _Builtin_intrinsics.sse
         -> xmmintrin.h
         -> mm_malloc.h      (Clang builtin)
         -> #include <stdlib.h>
            (resolved to libstdc++'s stdlib.h wrapper, which lives
             in the same directory as the injected modulemap)
            -> #include <cstdlib>
               (modular header, submodule std.compat.cstdlib)
               -> @import std  <-- currently being built

Clang rejects this with:

  stdlib.h:36:11: error: cyclic dependency in module 'std':
    std -> _Builtin_intrinsics -> std

aarch64 and armv7 don't hit this because <pmmintrin.h> is never
included by opt_random.h on non-x86 targets.

Mark cstdlib (and cassert, defensively) as textual rather than
modular. Per Clang's modules specification, including a textual
header does not trigger an import of the module that owns it; the
header's contents are expanded inline at the include site. So the
libstdc++ wrapper's #include <cstdlib> -- reached via mm_malloc ->
stdlib.h during the _Builtin_intrinsics build -- no longer re-enters
the currently-building std module.

The std.compat.{cstdlib,cassert} submodules are removed; a grep
across swift/stdlib, swift/lib/ClangImporter, and swift/test finds
no references to these qualified names, so nothing in-tree depends
on them being modular.

Upstream-Status: Submitted
---
 stdlib/public/Cxx/libstdcxx/libstdcxx.modulemap | 17 ++++-------------
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)

diff --git a/stdlib/public/Cxx/libstdcxx/libstdcxx.modulemap b/stdlib/public/Cxx/libstdcxx/libstdcxx.modulemap
--- a/stdlib/public/Cxx/libstdcxx/libstdcxx.modulemap
+++ b/stdlib/public/Cxx/libstdcxx/libstdcxx.modulemap
@@ -76,18 +76,9 @@ module std {
   requires cplusplus
   export *

-  /// C compatibility headers.
-  module compat {
-    module cassert {
-      header "cassert"
-      requires cplusplus
-      export *
-    }
-
-    module cstdlib {
-      header "cstdlib"
-      requires cplusplus
-      export *
-    }
-  }
+  /// C compatibility headers -- textual to break the
+  /// std -> _Builtin_intrinsics -> std cycle that fires on
+  /// x86_64 with -march>=x86-64-v3. See commit message.
+  textual header "cassert"
+  textual header "cstdlib"
 }
--
